 "result_text": "You can now play a specific chime sound. I haven't run the tests or tried it against a real chime.\n\nI added an optional `track_no` parameter in three places:\n- **API:** `play_speaker` in `src/uiprotect/api.py` sends the given `track_no` as `trackNo`. If you don't pass one, it still uses the chime's configured track, so the existing behaviour is unchanged.\n- **Chime object:** `Chime.play()` in `src/uiprotect/data/devices.py` passes `track_no` through.\n- **CLI:** the chime `play` command in `src/uiprotect/cli/chimes.py` has a new `-t` / `--track-no` option.\n\nPassing `track_no` on its own also uses the chime's current volume and repeat count. This doesn't change the sound configured for any paired doorbell.\n\nI didn't check which track numbers the built-in or uploaded sounds map to. The CLI accepts any number from 0 up.",
